From e2189952870517e31e4c8c5913cf0ccb2effc362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:11:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] pco, pvr: test descriptors once instead of guarding
 every access

zink enables robustBufferAccess and nullDescriptor for every GL context,
so every UBO load got a bounds check and every texture or image access a
branch on its descriptor being null. pco_nir_version_descriptor_checks()
tests once, at the start of the shader, whether any texture or image
descriptor it uses is null and whether any UBO is smaller than the
constant offsets read from it (a null UBO has size 0). If neither, a copy
of the shader without those checks runs; otherwise the original, fully
checked one. This is done only when every descriptor reference can be
rebuilt at the start and all outputs are stored at the top level, and not
for shaders over 3000 NIR instructions. Buffer null checks stay: the
robust clamp of a load from a null buffer still reads address 0.

UBO offsets are still "descriptor offset + constant" (unfolded) at this
point, so they are matched with nir_scalar_resolved() after constant
folding.

The two copies can push a shader over the register limit, and spilling
does not work (the shared registers holding the spill buffer address are
only reserved when spilled_temps is already known). So the pipeline
compile keeps each stage's NIR from before lowering and compiles a stage
again without versioning if it spilled (robustness2 storage_image
no_fmt_qual null_descriptor fragment cases did).

glmark2-es2 through zink, off-screen 800x600, FPS of two runs each,
before -> after: build 303/298 -> 368/360, phong 154/149 -> 206/209,
jellyfish 101/98 -> 136/139, terrain 8/8 -> 11/10; texture 589/555 ->
537/544 and effect2d 239/227 -> 232/240 within run-to-run noise.

CTS: robustness list (4025) 648 pass / 2 crash as before, 5062 list,
loops/indexing/graphicsfuzz list (6428), compute.pipeline (1235), TFBC
list (9170), synchronization (1718), dynamic_rendering sample (6745):
identical to before.
